WEBVTT

00:00:27.520 --> 00:00:31.490
I'll have to begin by explaining my work.

00:00:33.280 --> 00:00:38.910
The thing I require, before all else, is a corpse.

00:00:40.520 --> 00:00:44.140
London, 1878

00:00:52.670 --> 00:00:54.510
It's been confirmed that when a human dies,

00:00:54.720 --> 00:01:02.060
their body will then weigh 21 grams less than it did while alive.

00:01:02.270 --> 00:01:04.560
That's the weight of the spiritual element,

00:01:04.770 --> 00:01:07.110
the so-called weight of the soul.

00:01:09.770 --> 00:01:15.030
We reanimate the dead by installing pseudo spiritual elements

00:01:15.240 --> 00:01:17.200
in bodies that no longer have souls.

00:01:18.490 --> 00:01:21.950
They're nothing more than imitation souls, though.

00:01:27.460 --> 00:01:33.630
Dr. Victor Frankenstein gave life to the first corpse-- The One.

00:01:34.470 --> 00:01:37.970
It's said he could speak, desire love,

00:01:38.180 --> 00:01:40.430
and even feel the urge to commit murder.

00:01:41.930 --> 00:01:46.270
Then in a fit of despair, he took <i>Victor's Notes,</i>

00:01:46.480 --> 00:01:50.480
the technology that had given him life, and disappeared.

00:01:53.650 --> 00:01:55.570
All that was left to us were puppets,

00:01:55.780 --> 00:02:01.910
imitations of The One, with no souls or language.

00:02:04.120 --> 00:02:07.420
If The One had a soul...

00:02:07.620 --> 00:02:13.840
If a 21g soul can be put back inside an empty body,

00:02:14.050 --> 00:02:19.300
perhaps those we've lost can come back to us.

00:02:27.890 --> 00:02:29.310
Startup.

00:02:51.130 --> 00:02:53.840
Are you able to see me?

00:02:54.050 --> 00:02:56.550
Do you know who I am?

00:03:07.480 --> 00:03:08.890
Walk.

00:03:16.900 --> 00:03:18.400
Stop.

00:03:21.070 --> 00:03:24.120
No problems with the power system.

00:03:27.700 --> 00:03:29.330
Hold out your hand.

00:03:30.290 --> 00:03:31.830
Take this pen.

00:03:48.770 --> 00:03:51.600
Record every word and action.

00:03:53.190 --> 00:03:56.270
Hopefully that will become your soul.

00:03:58.440 --> 00:04:01.110
Welcome back, Friday.

00:04:09.200 --> 00:04:13.120
With the twentieth century not too far off,

00:04:13.330 --> 00:04:17.670
corpse technology has taken hold of the nation's destiny these days.

00:04:20.550 --> 00:04:27.390
Dr. Victor Frankenstein succeeded a century ago in reviving a corpse.

00:04:28.600 --> 00:04:34.690
People feared and abhorred the idea of resurrecting the dead.

00:04:34.900 --> 00:04:38.320
They made no attempt to embrace corpse technology.

00:04:41.570 --> 00:04:45.870
The first ones to accept the corpses were women.

00:04:47.410 --> 00:04:51.790
They would no longer have to lose their sons and husbands to war,

00:04:52.000 --> 00:04:54.540
if corpses could be used as soldiers.

00:04:56.420 --> 00:04:59.630
Corpse technology had a military application.

00:04:59.840 --> 00:05:05.590
Once the world realized this, its development proceeded apace.

00:05:10.220 --> 00:05:14.020
The new military technology found its way into the civilian realm,

00:05:14.230 --> 00:05:17.360
and revolutionized the way people lived.

00:05:19.900 --> 00:05:23.780
Simulations are run repeatedly on analytical engines,

00:05:23.990 --> 00:05:26.530
and pseudo spiritual elements recorded on punch cards

00:05:26.740 --> 00:05:29.280
are referred to as necroware.

00:05:29.490 --> 00:05:33.250
Corpses are optimized and adapted into coachmen, butlers,

00:05:33.450 --> 00:05:37.130
factory workers, and so on.

00:05:44.220 --> 00:05:49.260
The world is full of corpses, and it's no exaggeration to say

00:05:49.470 --> 00:05:54.270
they now carry the world economy on their shoulders.

00:05:57.690 --> 00:06:01.440
The old castle of terror, the Tower of London.

00:06:04.240 --> 00:06:09.370
Here, corpse engineers improve necroware on a daily basis,

00:06:09.570 --> 00:06:13.540
and continue to upgrade the contents of corpses worldwide.

00:06:14.910 --> 00:06:18.750
It's all by way of the eminent calculation abilities

00:06:18.960 --> 00:06:21.630
of the analytical engine Charles Babbage.

00:06:27.300 --> 00:06:30.930
This is a story about corpses.

00:06:55.370 --> 00:06:57.160
A Cambridge Engine,

00:06:57.370 --> 00:07:01.500
and an expanded Edinburgh language dual spiritual element analyzer.

00:07:01.710 --> 00:07:05.460
You really got through a lot in a short time.

00:07:05.670 --> 00:07:07.800
I'm impressed.

00:07:10.720 --> 00:07:12.010
However.

00:07:12.220 --> 00:07:16.220
As I'm sure you're aware, spiritual element analysis is a state secret.

00:07:17.060 --> 00:07:20.270
If you know this is a serious crime,

00:07:20.480 --> 00:07:24.190
what are you trying to accomplish with this risky business?

00:07:25.610 --> 00:07:28.240
The bereaved family is sure to grieve all the more,

00:07:28.440 --> 00:07:32.490
once they learn a close friend of the deceased stole his body.

00:07:33.950 --> 00:07:37.620
The gossip papers won't keep quiet about it, either.

00:07:37.830 --> 00:07:43.130
"The abnormal affections of an outstanding London University medical student."

00:07:43.330 --> 00:07:47.760
Unauthorized corpse reanimation, and the installation of illegal necroware.

00:07:47.960 --> 00:07:50.470
You'll serve jail time for this.

00:07:54.640 --> 00:07:58.100
Do you think I never expected to get caught?

00:08:00.390 --> 00:08:02.350
All right, then.

00:08:02.560 --> 00:08:04.730
Her Majesty the Queen isn't so ignorant

00:08:04.940 --> 00:08:10.570
that she'd let this much talent and passion rot in a hole in the ground.

00:08:13.200 --> 00:08:16.530
Let's make a deal, shall we?

00:08:16.740 --> 00:08:18.830
My name is M.

00:08:19.040 --> 00:08:24.670
It's time you did some work for the British Empire, John Watson.

00:08:52.800 --> 00:08:57.340
Bombay, British Indian Empire, 1878

00:09:08.250 --> 00:09:12.130
The former American president, Ulysses Grant.

00:09:13.220 --> 00:09:15.590
He must be going around in person, marketing the technology

00:09:15.800 --> 00:09:18.430
they cultivated during the Civil War.

00:09:27.730 --> 00:09:31.110
What just happened? What exploded?

00:09:39.870 --> 00:09:41.910
Look alive, schoolboy.

00:09:43.540 --> 00:09:45.080
What're you doing?!

00:09:45.290 --> 00:09:49.420
Don't want to die as soon as you reach the battlefield, do you?

00:09:49.630 --> 00:09:51.050
Let's go!

00:10:08.020 --> 00:10:10.560
Shake him off! He'll explode!

00:10:11.860 --> 00:10:14.360
Friday! Do something!

00:10:18.820 --> 00:10:20.320
Damn it!

00:10:24.040 --> 00:10:25.910
What are they, anyway?

00:10:26.120 --> 00:10:28.290
Russian-made corpse bombs.

00:10:28.500 --> 00:10:33.420
Instead of carrying a bomb around, the corpse itself is the bomb.

00:10:33.630 --> 00:10:36.800
So, it dissolved fat into glycerin.

00:10:37.010 --> 00:10:38.340
That's impressive.

00:10:38.550 --> 00:10:42.050
No time for admiration. We've got more company!

00:10:44.140 --> 00:10:46.350
Get inside and hold on tight!

00:10:49.270 --> 00:10:51.480
Looks like the Russians are frantic.

00:10:59.110 --> 00:11:01.280
Why're we being shot at?!

00:11:01.490 --> 00:11:05.290
It means we're not the only ones after the treasure.

00:11:05.490 --> 00:11:08.370
Friday, get the gun out of the bag!

00:11:25.560 --> 00:11:26.720
Hurry and throw him off!

00:11:26.930 --> 00:11:29.440
Friday, shoot this guy!

00:11:31.310 --> 00:11:36.030
Friday! Use that gun in your hand, and shoot this guy in the head!

00:11:40.700 --> 00:11:42.160
Shoot!

00:11:53.000 --> 00:11:54.540
They don't give up.

00:11:54.750 --> 00:11:56.300
Switch with me!

00:11:56.500 --> 00:11:57.510
Switch?!

00:11:57.710 --> 00:12:00.930
Just sit here, and hold the reins.

00:12:01.130 --> 00:12:03.220
Easy for you to say!

00:12:21.490 --> 00:12:23.530
That takes care of that.

00:12:23.740 --> 00:12:28.200
You're Burnaby, aren't you? Captain Frederick Burnaby.

00:12:28.410 --> 00:12:32.160
The guide Walsingham arranged. Or rather, the watchdog.

00:12:32.370 --> 00:12:34.540
Those're both wrong.

00:12:34.750 --> 00:12:38.210
I'm a baby-sitter for the stupid death-obsessed schoolboy.

00:12:39.880 --> 00:12:41.420
Ah, don't get so mad.

00:12:41.630 --> 00:12:43.630
Worst case, I'll bring back your corpse

00:12:43.840 --> 00:12:45.510
like I did your predecessor's.

00:12:45.720 --> 00:12:48.180
Even corpses can work for their country, these days.

00:12:48.390 --> 00:12:50.600
Predecessor? What are you talking about?

00:12:50.810 --> 00:12:55.020
He got blown away by a bomb. That's why they sent you.

00:12:55.230 --> 00:12:56.150
I wasn't told this!

00:12:56.360 --> 00:13:01.320
Must have slipped their minds. Well, he had bad luck.

00:13:01.530 --> 00:13:04.660
Here's hoping you've got good luck.

00:13:04.860 --> 00:13:08.700
Oh, that's right. Write down that I'm good-looking.

00:13:08.910 --> 00:13:10.830
You don't have to write that, Friday.

00:13:11.870 --> 00:13:14.290
Oh come on, let him do his job.

00:13:14.500 --> 00:13:16.710
<i>You're</i> the one making it difficult.

00:13:31.060 --> 00:13:33.180
There sure are a lot of soldiers.

00:13:33.390 --> 00:13:38.310
The old style Krishna Engine... and the Carabinieri Engine?

00:13:38.520 --> 00:13:41.070
That's because they're sending them to Afghanistan.

00:13:41.280 --> 00:13:44.740
From here on, there'll be more dead people than living.

00:13:44.950 --> 00:13:48.490
Might be a fun place for a corpse engineer like you.

00:13:52.620 --> 00:13:53.750
You can't have any.

00:13:53.950 --> 00:13:55.330
I don't want any.

00:13:55.540 --> 00:13:58.420
Oops, I've got something to give you.

00:13:58.630 --> 00:14:00.380
Here.

00:14:00.590 --> 00:14:01.500
What is it?

00:14:01.710 --> 00:14:03.170
It's from Walsingham.

00:14:03.380 --> 00:14:04.510
Identity documents?

00:14:04.720 --> 00:14:06.340
Forged ones, yeah.

00:14:09.470 --> 00:14:12.680
You're a doctor of medicine. An army surgeon.

00:14:12.890 --> 00:14:15.730
Not that I've even graduated yet.

00:14:17.520 --> 00:14:19.610
This man...

00:14:19.810 --> 00:14:22.730
Aleksei Fyodorovich Karamazov.

00:14:24.440 --> 00:14:27.240
An Imperial Russian Army chaplain...

00:14:27.450 --> 00:14:30.700
And, the man touted to be the Dr. Frankenstein

00:14:30.910 --> 00:14:32.660
of the Romanov dynasty?

00:14:34.330 --> 00:14:38.120
Three months ago, that corpse engineer led a band

00:14:38.330 --> 00:14:42.040
of armed corpses in an uprising,

00:14:42.250 --> 00:14:46.050
and disappeared into the wilds of Afghanistan.

00:14:46.260 --> 00:14:47.720
What was his goal?

00:14:47.930 --> 00:14:52.140
The establishment of a new kingdom, with corpses as its subjects.

00:14:52.350 --> 00:14:56.100
Rather than go to prison, you want me to infiltrate Afghanistan

00:14:56.310 --> 00:15:00.520
in the middle of a war, and investigate this so-called kingdom?

00:15:03.900 --> 00:15:10.860
Karamazov is carrying Dr. Victor Frankenstein's lost research notes.

00:15:11.070 --> 00:15:13.200
<i>Victor's Notes...</i>

00:15:13.410 --> 00:15:18.250
They say The One was the only corpse who acquired a soul and was able to speak.

00:15:18.460 --> 00:15:22.210
The technology that produced him is there?

00:15:22.420 --> 00:15:27.170
The Russian emperor's own Third Secretariat is on the move, too.

00:15:27.380 --> 00:15:28.970
It's The Great Game.

00:15:29.170 --> 00:15:36.180
We can't let the Russian Empire <i>or</i> Karamazov dominate the world.

00:15:36.390 --> 00:15:41.520
Investigate the corpse kingdom, and secure <i>Victor's Notes.</i>

00:15:41.730 --> 00:15:44.480
That's your mission.

00:15:56.700 --> 00:16:01.370
You're very late in arriving. I thought maybe you'd died.

00:16:01.580 --> 00:16:03.420
Things came up.

00:16:03.630 --> 00:16:08.550
I guess they don't teach you to be punctual, in Great Britain.

00:16:08.760 --> 00:16:12.930
You're a smart-aleck brat, as always.

00:16:13.140 --> 00:16:16.600
Nice to meet you. I'm Nikolai Krasotkin.

00:16:16.810 --> 00:16:19.520
I'm Watson. John Watson.

00:16:19.730 --> 00:16:25.020
The mad engineer who willfully turned his friend into a corpse.

00:16:25.230 --> 00:16:31.320
Well, circumstances aside, I have high hopes for you, Dr. Watson.

00:16:31.530 --> 00:16:33.240
This way, please.

00:16:34.490 --> 00:16:38.910
He's Russian, isn't he? His people nearly killed us in Bombay!

00:16:39.120 --> 00:16:42.410
Don't worry, he's working with us.

00:16:42.620 --> 00:16:43.830
He's our guide.

00:16:44.040 --> 00:16:46.880
Can we trust him?! Hey, Burnaby!

00:16:47.090 --> 00:16:51.170
Karamazov acquired new technology from the <i>Notes</i>.

00:16:51.380 --> 00:16:53.550
Don't you want to see it?

00:17:03.810 --> 00:17:05.770
Let's go, Friday.

00:17:19.950 --> 00:17:22.580
You guys are after the <i>Notes</i> too, aren't you?

00:17:22.790 --> 00:17:25.250
Why take part in a joint operation?

00:17:25.460 --> 00:17:29.960
You don't need to worry. I'll let you have the <i>Notes</i>.

00:17:30.170 --> 00:17:35.970
If we can secure Karamazov himself, that'll be good enough for us.

00:17:36.180 --> 00:17:41.810
Aha. So things are a mess within the Russian Empire, too.

00:17:42.020 --> 00:17:45.850
If we're after different results, how we go about it varies as well.

00:17:46.060 --> 00:17:48.310
That's all there is to it.

00:17:50.270 --> 00:17:52.780
Well, it's a long trip.

00:17:52.990 --> 00:17:55.780
Let's all us agents just get along.

00:18:10.960 --> 00:18:13.510
All right, try reloading.

00:18:25.480 --> 00:18:28.020
That's quite daring.

00:18:28.230 --> 00:18:30.020
It's a self-defense measure.

00:18:30.230 --> 00:18:32.440
His cognition is inferior to a human's,

00:18:32.650 --> 00:18:35.030
but he's excellent at not hesitating.

00:18:35.240 --> 00:18:39.110
I pray you're not the one who gets shot.

00:18:40.620 --> 00:18:44.240
Are you and Aleksei Karamazov from the same region, or something?

00:18:44.450 --> 00:18:46.870
It's like it says in the documents I provided you.

00:18:48.210 --> 00:18:52.880
He stole the <i>Notes</i> in the middle of a military corpse experiment.

00:18:53.090 --> 00:18:55.920
Along with some of the test subjects.

00:18:56.130 --> 00:18:59.430
Did he succeed in reproducing The One?

00:18:59.640 --> 00:19:01.220
What was in the formula?

00:19:01.430 --> 00:19:05.850
That is to say, he <i>did</i> finish his analysis of the formula?

00:19:06.060 --> 00:19:07.560
Who can say?

00:19:07.770 --> 00:19:13.440
Maybe he plans to create a group of killers like the ancient Assassins.

00:19:13.650 --> 00:19:15.650
That's what the higher-ups suspect,

00:19:15.860 --> 00:19:19.570
so they're trying in secret to put a stop to all this.

00:19:19.780 --> 00:19:25.790
But you guys claim you can't allow Karamazov to be killed.

00:19:25.990 --> 00:19:30.080
What's he doing up in those secluded mountains?

00:19:30.290 --> 00:19:31.710
If it's something that serves our national interests,

00:19:31.920 --> 00:19:33.920
we'll need to bring it back home.

00:19:35.130 --> 00:19:39.630
He's currently in the Kokcha River valley, north of Kabul.

00:19:39.840 --> 00:19:44.640
If you know that much, why do you need to team up with us?

00:19:44.850 --> 00:19:51.020
Because we need you, Dr. Watson.

00:19:51.230 --> 00:19:56.320
Someone like yourself, who's well versed in corpse technology.

00:20:02.070 --> 00:20:03.490
Fire!

00:20:06.300 --> 00:20:10.270
Khyber Pass, 1878

00:20:10.750 --> 00:20:12.170
Fire!

00:20:15.040 --> 00:20:19.010
It's a waste if they don't draw the enemy closer before shooting.

00:20:19.210 --> 00:20:20.670
Let them shoot.

00:20:24.930 --> 00:20:28.350
With them facing that many corpse soldiers,

00:20:28.560 --> 00:20:31.390
wouldn't it be cruel to expect any self-control?

00:20:37.320 --> 00:20:42.070
A single numerical formula will predict victory or defeat.

00:20:42.280 --> 00:20:44.450
Where's the need to actually fight?

00:20:45.410 --> 00:20:48.910
Then it would become just a game.

00:20:49.120 --> 00:20:52.410
People need stories.

00:20:52.620 --> 00:20:58.710
Stories adorned with words that make the blood stir and the flesh leap.

00:20:58.920 --> 00:21:02.800
The majority of people can't understand your rationale.

00:21:03.010 --> 00:21:07.510
Those who can't understand, can't accept.

00:21:07.720 --> 00:21:11.180
Other than things they can touch or see, that is.

00:21:11.390 --> 00:21:17.610
Stories are born of our foolishness, which they then continuously affirm.

00:21:19.020 --> 00:21:22.400
And so, this is the result.

00:21:27.370 --> 00:21:30.740
It looks a bit easier to walk here.

00:21:30.950 --> 00:21:32.330
Don't relax.

00:21:32.540 --> 00:21:35.210
The enemy can easily see us here.

00:21:35.420 --> 00:21:39.000
You really will die, if you're careless.

00:21:44.510 --> 00:21:46.510
We've got trouble! Get clear!

00:21:51.180 --> 00:21:54.640
This might be the first fun fight I've had in a while.

00:21:57.400 --> 00:21:59.520
You need to stay back.

00:21:59.730 --> 00:22:02.110
Friday, get your gun ready.

00:22:21.750 --> 00:22:26.090
Unbelievable. He anticipated my damn movements.

00:22:26.300 --> 00:22:28.930
Is this guy really a corpse?

00:22:30.510 --> 00:22:31.930
He dodged?!

00:22:38.730 --> 00:22:42.690
So, my country really did deploy it after all.

00:22:44.230 --> 00:22:48.780
Dr. Watson! That's the necroware Karamazov developed!

00:22:52.950 --> 00:22:57.620
Dexterity, and the ability to move each joint in a coordinated manner.

00:22:57.830 --> 00:22:59.330
The ability to grasp the situation,

00:22:59.540 --> 00:23:02.840
and anticipate well enough to select the best option.

00:23:03.050 --> 00:23:06.550
All those things set them apart from preexisting corpses.

00:23:06.760 --> 00:23:09.010
They have the urge to kill!

00:23:09.220 --> 00:23:11.680
The emotion of murderous intent...

00:23:17.730 --> 00:23:22.480
That's where we'll find Victor's prized technology!

00:23:26.940 --> 00:23:28.650
There's no end of them.

00:24:14.160 --> 00:24:15.990
Watson! Hurry up!

00:24:16.200 --> 00:24:17.330
This is no time for love.

00:24:17.540 --> 00:24:19.120
It's nothing like that!

00:24:25.170 --> 00:24:28.260
This is... our only option?

00:24:28.460 --> 00:24:31.380
Just this. Now get going.

00:24:32.300 --> 00:24:35.390
Do you want that woman's rescue to be for nothing?

00:24:35.600 --> 00:24:37.180
All right.

00:24:38.520 --> 00:24:39.310
Burnaby!

00:24:39.520 --> 00:24:41.390
If it's a last request, save it.

00:24:43.020 --> 00:24:47.020
Can we grab that new model?

00:24:47.230 --> 00:24:48.650
Huh?

00:25:20.970 --> 00:25:23.890
Power up the installer.

00:25:26.270 --> 00:25:32.070
Did that killing urge I sensed belong to this corpse himself?

00:25:32.280 --> 00:25:38.870
Or is it nothing more than a variation in his installed program?

00:25:39.080 --> 00:25:41.120
Does he possess language?

00:25:41.330 --> 00:25:43.500
Where is his soul?

00:25:44.580 --> 00:25:46.040
Startup.

00:25:55.130 --> 00:25:57.300
Increase the thought control system's load.

00:26:07.020 --> 00:26:09.980
Yes, that's the look!

00:26:16.490 --> 00:26:18.700
Can you speak?

00:26:21.330 --> 00:26:24.000
Increase the output, Friday!

00:26:27.370 --> 00:26:28.580
What's your name?

00:26:28.790 --> 00:26:31.800
Tell me! Your name!

00:26:52.770 --> 00:26:56.490
We're halting the experiment, Friday.

00:27:09.870 --> 00:27:13.460
Why do you ask a corpse its name?

00:27:13.670 --> 00:27:15.380
What are you trying to say?

00:27:15.590 --> 00:27:18.880
Does it have something to do with your friend?

00:27:20.050 --> 00:27:23.180
Noble_Savage_007.

00:27:23.390 --> 00:27:28.390
That's Friday's registration name, as property of Walsingham.

00:27:28.600 --> 00:27:31.690
Corpses are always given an ID number.

00:27:31.900 --> 00:27:35.940
They're left with a name, a symbolic identity.

00:27:36.150 --> 00:27:37.690
If you analyze their ID,

00:27:37.900 --> 00:27:40.700
won't that simply tell you their basic properties?

00:27:40.910 --> 00:27:44.740
Corpses don't need names, and they can't speak.

00:27:46.080 --> 00:27:49.620
For what reason do you seek the <i>Notes</i>?

00:27:53.630 --> 00:27:55.920
That's how engineers are, isn't it?

00:27:56.130 --> 00:27:59.050
I bet it's the same where you're from.

00:28:01.720 --> 00:28:05.180
Technical innovation is like an instinct for them.

00:28:07.600 --> 00:28:11.350
Things might've been easier if he'd been able to see it that simply.

00:28:39.010 --> 00:28:42.340
The <i>Notes</i> might be the real thing, Friday.

00:28:44.470 --> 00:28:47.600
Maybe we'll be able to prove your theory.

00:28:51.730 --> 00:28:54.730
Dr. Watson, I presume.

00:28:54.940 --> 00:28:59.780
I'm Hadaly, President Grant's private secretary.

00:28:59.980 --> 00:29:02.610
You bailed us out earlier.

00:29:03.570 --> 00:29:07.080
President Grant is fond of danger.

00:29:15.000 --> 00:29:17.880
Was there a soul?

00:29:18.090 --> 00:29:21.590
That corpse earlier moved exactly like the living,

00:29:21.800 --> 00:29:23.630
and it still had intelligence.

00:29:23.840 --> 00:29:25.930
So did it have a soul?

00:29:26.140 --> 00:29:31.060
My friend would often say that thought precedes language.

00:29:31.270 --> 00:29:35.940
And that corpse was trying to say something.

00:29:36.150 --> 00:29:42.440
In other words, maybe the soul is hidden behind thought?

00:29:42.650 --> 00:29:47.910
It's currently nothing more than a hypothesis, but I mean to prove it.

00:29:49.240 --> 00:29:53.290
Perhaps your soul desires that?

00:29:55.460 --> 00:29:59.340
Souls don't seem real to me.

00:30:00.840 --> 00:30:04.050
I don't know what they're like.

00:30:04.970 --> 00:30:08.010
Maybe I'm similar to this one here.

00:30:11.970 --> 00:30:14.390
Until we meet again, somewhere.

00:30:28.070 --> 00:30:31.700
A woman like her is a lot for you to handle.

00:30:31.910 --> 00:30:33.450
Be careful.

00:32:35.830 --> 00:32:41.160
Why did Karamazov steal the corpse soldiers and cause an uprising?

00:32:41.370 --> 00:32:43.500
From what I've seen of the new model corpses,

00:32:43.710 --> 00:32:47.500
he must have been close to reproducing The One.

00:32:47.710 --> 00:32:50.130
Does there have to be a reason?

00:32:50.340 --> 00:32:53.640
At least then I could understand.

00:32:53.840 --> 00:32:57.100
I thought your mission was to secure the <i>Notes</i>,

00:32:57.310 --> 00:33:00.980
not to learn the cause of what happened, or the reasons.

00:33:03.440 --> 00:33:08.190
As for Alyosha's story, you can ask him about it firsthand.

00:33:09.980 --> 00:33:11.490
We're here.

00:33:29.090 --> 00:33:31.670
Woman and child corpses!

00:33:44.850 --> 00:33:48.690
I've been awaiting you, Dr. Watson.

00:33:48.900 --> 00:33:51.440
I am Aleksei Karamazov.

00:33:56.450 --> 00:33:59.910
I'm happy to see you're in good health, Alyosha.

00:34:00.120 --> 00:34:03.200
You've done well, Kolya.

00:34:03.410 --> 00:34:05.330
Thank goodness you got here in time.

00:34:05.540 --> 00:34:11.920
If his task was to bring us here, I wish he had picked an easier route.

00:34:12.130 --> 00:34:16.300
The British Empire is very concerned about this situation.

00:34:16.510 --> 00:34:19.350
I'd like to ask you about your intentions.

00:34:23.890 --> 00:34:27.350
Nikolai and I discovered it.

00:34:27.560 --> 00:34:31.400
On an island in the Arctic we visited while on a mission.

00:34:33.070 --> 00:34:35.650
Dr. Watson.

00:34:35.860 --> 00:34:39.620
Why is it you seek the <i>Notes</i>?

00:34:39.820 --> 00:34:43.870
To reproduce The One? Or perhaps because your nation ordered it?

00:34:44.080 --> 00:34:47.330
The pursuit of corpse technology doesn't require any great cause.

00:34:49.080 --> 00:34:52.300
I too once repeatedly performed corpse experiments

00:34:52.500 --> 00:34:55.260
in an effort to reproduce The One.

00:34:55.470 --> 00:35:00.010
Piles of countless corpses; light that faded from countless eyes.

00:35:00.220 --> 00:35:06.350
When I noticed myself reflected in those eyes, I came to my senses.

00:35:06.560 --> 00:35:10.310
I wondered, what had I been seeking?

00:35:13.520 --> 00:35:19.700
I'll ask again. Why is it you seek the <i>Notes</i>?

00:35:19.910 --> 00:35:21.870
The advancement of corpse technology.

00:35:22.070 --> 00:35:24.740
The reproduction of The One.

00:35:24.950 --> 00:35:29.000
Even if that means dabbling in the taboo?

00:35:29.210 --> 00:35:33.460
Even taboo techniques must someday become commonplace.

00:35:34.590 --> 00:35:37.670
Corpses are part of our everyday lives, at this point.

00:35:37.880 --> 00:35:39.970
You're probably right.

00:35:40.180 --> 00:35:41.930
Once a technology comes into existence,

00:35:42.140 --> 00:35:45.220
no one can halt it for his own convenience.

00:35:45.430 --> 00:35:49.190
That's why Nikolai and I got rid of the data,

00:35:49.390 --> 00:35:53.310
and overwrote crucial sections.

00:35:53.520 --> 00:35:57.780
The Empire has put new model corpses on the battlefield.

00:35:57.990 --> 00:36:01.110
The world will probably undergo a rapid reorganization.

00:36:02.110 --> 00:36:05.200
Great Britain won't keep quiet.

00:36:05.410 --> 00:36:07.910
Where are the <i>Notes</i>?

00:36:08.120 --> 00:36:12.830
If you seek the <i>Notes</i>, please promise me you'll destroy them.

00:36:13.040 --> 00:36:14.090
Why?!

00:36:14.290 --> 00:36:15.960
There's no need for a reason.

00:36:16.170 --> 00:36:19.800
The many words you've accumulated thus far

00:36:20.010 --> 00:36:23.220
will most likely determine your story.

00:36:44.070 --> 00:36:45.530
Friday...

00:37:11.230 --> 00:37:15.690
He must be the reason you pursue the <i>Notes</i>.

00:37:15.900 --> 00:37:19.610
You aren't treating him like property.

00:37:22.400 --> 00:37:27.330
Dr. Watson, are you prepared to be responsible for the reality

00:37:27.530 --> 00:37:31.000
that lies beyond the technology in the <i>Notes</i>?

00:37:31.200 --> 00:37:36.500
Whatever reality lies in wait, I <i>will</i> get my hands on the <i>Notes</i>.

00:37:39.050 --> 00:37:44.340
Those are the words you've arrived at on this journey.

00:37:46.050 --> 00:37:48.600
I'm glad I got to talk to you.

00:37:48.800 --> 00:37:50.140
Likewise.

00:37:50.350 --> 00:37:52.810
See you tomorrow, then.

00:38:24.670 --> 00:38:26.970
Friday, come with me.

00:38:50.620 --> 00:38:54.250
You are not allowed to avert your eyes.

00:38:54.450 --> 00:38:59.210
This is the new corpse technology you sought!

00:39:00.630 --> 00:39:02.090
Stop!

00:39:04.260 --> 00:39:06.050
Nikolai!

00:39:06.260 --> 00:39:07.930
I'll get this off you!

00:39:09.640 --> 00:39:11.050
Damn it!

00:39:25.820 --> 00:39:35.820
Now my... duty to... you is... done...

00:39:41.670 --> 00:39:46.760
No... Writing a pseudo spiritual element onto a living person...

00:39:46.960 --> 00:39:49.300
It shouldn't be possible!

00:39:52.890 --> 00:39:54.600
Opium, huh?

00:39:54.810 --> 00:39:57.600
Entrancing music is also important.

00:39:57.810 --> 00:40:01.440
You produce an artificially muddled trance,

00:40:01.650 --> 00:40:04.480
then anchor it with a pseudo spiritual element.

00:40:04.690 --> 00:40:07.030
That's the method recorded in the <i>Notes</i>.

00:40:07.230 --> 00:40:10.860
That's insane. It's just murder!

00:40:11.070 --> 00:40:13.160
You're no different!

00:40:13.370 --> 00:40:16.450
You vivisected a living man in the Khyber Pass.

00:40:16.660 --> 00:40:19.500
He was the same as Nikolai, here!

00:40:28.090 --> 00:40:32.840
I experimented on my older brother.

00:40:33.050 --> 00:40:35.640
You and I are similar to one another.

00:40:35.850 --> 00:40:38.520
In our quest to reproduce The One,

00:40:38.720 --> 00:40:42.440
we made tools even of those dear to us.

00:40:46.440 --> 00:40:49.690
Where is... Nikolai's soul?!

00:40:50.950 --> 00:40:53.160
There is no soul.

00:40:53.360 --> 00:40:57.700
We merely overwrite the future with death.

00:40:58.950 --> 00:41:03.620
Now do you understand how foolish this technology is?

00:41:05.750 --> 00:41:09.000
The technology's just incomplete!

00:41:10.970 --> 00:41:13.300
Why didn't you move forward?

00:41:15.140 --> 00:41:17.010
If you'd only charged ahead,

00:41:17.220 --> 00:41:20.680
you might have found the soul waiting just beyond!

00:41:22.480 --> 00:41:25.480
How can we sacrifice someone dear to us,

00:41:25.690 --> 00:41:28.730
then pretend it never happened?!

00:41:29.820 --> 00:41:32.400
<i>You're</i> the one who averted his eyes!

00:41:47.040 --> 00:41:52.460
It truly is difficult to convey one's thoughts to another.

00:42:00.680 --> 00:42:03.930
Please forgive me, Nikolai.

00:42:05.060 --> 00:42:06.690
Brother...

00:42:08.810 --> 00:42:12.070
There was no other way but this.

00:42:18.370 --> 00:42:23.120
Right now, the <i>Notes</i>... are in Japan.

00:42:23.330 --> 00:42:26.830
If you mean to move forward, then do so.

00:42:29.960 --> 00:42:37.430
But when you do find the <i>Notes</i>... I just want you to recall my words.

00:42:39.140 --> 00:42:44.350
We want the <i>Notes</i> to be destroyed.

00:42:47.690 --> 00:42:49.400
I...!

00:43:20.050 --> 00:43:21.930
Russia had issued assassination orders

00:43:22.140 --> 00:43:25.430
against Nikolai and Karamazov.

00:43:25.640 --> 00:43:28.020
The only thing they could do in what little time they had left

00:43:28.230 --> 00:43:32.820
was bet on your good sense as a corpse engineer.

00:43:35.610 --> 00:43:42.700
Why didn't Karamazov... destroy the <i>Notes</i> himself?

00:43:42.910 --> 00:43:46.870
It's just like how you can't destroy Friday.

00:43:47.080 --> 00:43:48.870
I'm going to Japan.

00:43:50.040 --> 00:43:52.540
What will you tell Walsingham?

00:43:52.750 --> 00:43:54.960
That I'm continuing to pursue the <i>Notes</i>.

00:43:57.760 --> 00:43:59.840
Won't that be good enough?

00:44:00.050 --> 00:44:03.720
After seeing all that, I can't just pretend I didn't know him.

00:44:03.930 --> 00:44:08.680
He was sarcastic as hell, but we drank together.

00:44:08.890 --> 00:44:14.110
We laughed, and joked around a little too.

00:44:14.320 --> 00:44:16.940
I can at least destroy it for him.

00:44:27.910 --> 00:44:31.040
Let's go to Japan.

00:45:18.230 --> 00:45:22.030
Tokyo, 1879

00:45:22.050 --> 00:45:23.070
Full   house

00:45:23.510 --> 00:45:32.060
Now, for today's final bout!

00:45:35.900 --> 00:45:37.650
Pardon me, sir.

00:45:39.980 --> 00:45:42.280
Are you British?

00:45:42.490 --> 00:45:44.280
I am most indebted to the British Empire,

00:45:44.490 --> 00:45:48.410
on account of the recent Russo-Turkish War.

00:45:48.620 --> 00:45:50.540
- And go! Keep going! Keep going!
- I was sent there as an observer,

00:45:50.540 --> 00:45:55.830
- And go! Keep going! Keep going!
- and I witnessed, from the Russian side, the Siege of Plevna.

00:45:56.040 --> 00:46:01.260
But the truth is, the British Empire never advanced into Plevna.

00:46:03.510 --> 00:46:06.590
Well, we'll just leave it at that.

00:46:11.770 --> 00:46:13.270
Keep going!

00:46:13.480 --> 00:46:15.100
The winner!

00:46:19.480 --> 00:46:23.240
I was dispatched by the Ministry of Foreign Affairs,

00:46:23.440 --> 00:46:29.490
at the request of a comrade of Mr. Nikolai Krasotkin.

00:46:29.700 --> 00:46:32.790
I am Seigo Yamazawa, of the Imperial Japanese Army.

00:46:33.000 --> 00:46:36.870
Your companion is waiting outside. This way, if you please.

00:46:46.130 --> 00:46:48.300
What have you been up to?

00:46:48.510 --> 00:46:50.550
An undercover investigation.

00:46:50.760 --> 00:46:52.680
And what have you found?

00:46:52.680 --> 00:46:54.240
#1

00:46:52.890 --> 00:46:55.020
I got caught right away.

00:46:55.230 --> 00:46:56.690
So nothing, really.

00:46:57.770 --> 00:47:01.270
Aren't you embarrassed, dressed like that?

00:47:01.480 --> 00:47:03.610
It's not underwear, so I'm not embarrassed.

00:47:03.820 --> 00:47:08.070
All right. If it works for you, that's fine by me.

00:47:12.240 --> 00:47:13.450
The <i>Notes</i> are gone?

00:47:13.660 --> 00:47:15.580
They were entrusted by Mr. Karamazov

00:47:15.790 --> 00:47:17.920
to the previous minister to Russia,

00:47:18.120 --> 00:47:20.670
and <i>he</i> had them until he returned to Japan,

00:47:20.880 --> 00:47:26.470
but the last we've heard is that he made contact with Osato Chemicals.

00:47:27.220 --> 00:47:29.050
What is Osato Chemicals?

00:47:29.260 --> 00:47:31.510
It's a corporation linked with the old government

00:47:31.720 --> 00:47:34.310
that devotes itself to developing corpse technology,

00:47:34.520 --> 00:47:38.350
but at one point it began keeping all its business affairs secret.

00:47:38.560 --> 00:47:42.480
Did that happen to be when it acquired the <i>Notes</i>?

00:47:42.690 --> 00:47:45.690
I should also point out that it plans to develop new corpse models

00:47:45.900 --> 00:47:50.570
in an effort to win influence back from the new government.

00:47:50.780 --> 00:47:52.740
This is getting dicey.

00:47:52.950 --> 00:47:54.450
So what?

00:47:55.870 --> 00:47:58.580
Seems more interesting that way.

00:48:16.810 --> 00:48:18.560
Excuse me, sir.

00:48:18.770 --> 00:48:21.850
Dr. Watson is in Japan, after all.

00:48:23.360 --> 00:48:25.230
Captain Burnaby is with him, too.

00:48:30.780 --> 00:48:32.990
You had anticipated this, sir?

00:48:34.120 --> 00:48:37.660
Predicting the future is my job, after all.

00:49:08.610 --> 00:49:11.650
The guards on duty are nearly all knocked out.

00:49:11.860 --> 00:49:13.740
We should be all right for a while.

00:49:13.950 --> 00:49:17.990
There are signs of unauthorized access to Research Building 2.

00:49:19.120 --> 00:49:20.790
Someone beat us to it?

00:49:21.000 --> 00:49:22.790
It was 23 minutes ago.

00:49:23.000 --> 00:49:24.500
I'd say it's possible.

00:49:35.090 --> 00:49:36.760
There are no guards to be seen.

00:49:36.970 --> 00:49:40.720
Living people have been killed. This has to be a trap.

00:49:40.930 --> 00:49:41.810
Want to come back later?

00:49:42.020 --> 00:49:44.650
No, let's accept the invitation.

00:49:49.070 --> 00:49:51.610
Attacking the unarmed...

00:49:55.570 --> 00:49:59.870
I can see the <i>Notes</i> have quite an appeal.

00:50:07.710 --> 00:50:09.880
Maybe this is who got here first?

00:50:10.090 --> 00:50:15.300
Yeah, he's a Walsingham agent. I'm sure of it.

00:50:15.510 --> 00:50:20.810
It looks like someone besides us and Britain is after the <i>Notes</i>.

00:50:38.870 --> 00:50:41.490
What do you suppose these spots are?

00:50:41.700 --> 00:50:44.500
They probably inoculated living people with pathogens.

00:50:44.710 --> 00:50:47.250
Once their cerebral functions were adversely affected,

00:50:47.460 --> 00:50:49.420
they wrote in pseudo spiritual elements.

00:50:49.630 --> 00:50:54.170
Biological weapons that spread germs, eh?

00:50:54.380 --> 00:50:56.880
That's a screwed-up way to use them.

00:50:57.090 --> 00:50:59.800
Let's hurry up and destroy the <i>Notes</i>.

00:51:00.010 --> 00:51:02.060
There'll be more of the dead.

00:51:36.210 --> 00:51:39.760
This isn't good. I can tell they're experts.

00:51:39.970 --> 00:51:42.050
It's probably some Musoken style.

00:51:43.260 --> 00:51:47.230
I don't know what "Muso" is, but this works for me!

00:52:02.160 --> 00:52:03.700
Stand back, please!

00:52:26.640 --> 00:52:29.100
This finishes it!

00:52:46.030 --> 00:52:47.830
Watson, we've got this!

00:52:48.040 --> 00:52:50.250
You go and destroy the <i>Notes</i>!

00:52:55.710 --> 00:52:57.130
Watson!

00:53:04.340 --> 00:53:05.760
Go!

00:53:06.260 --> 00:53:08.220
Destroy the <i>Notes</i>!

00:53:08.430 --> 00:53:09.850
Thank you!

00:53:16.650 --> 00:53:18.820
Let's go, Friday.

00:53:31.410 --> 00:53:34.960
Friday, look for <i>Victor's Notes</i>.

00:53:59.730 --> 00:54:02.360
This is...

00:54:02.570 --> 00:54:04.570
<i>Victor's Notes</i>...

00:54:16.540 --> 00:54:19.000
Thought precedes language.

00:54:20.960 --> 00:54:24.510
If there's language, there's a mind.

00:54:24.720 --> 00:54:27.010
That's where the soul is.

00:54:30.100 --> 00:54:34.350
Prove to them the 21g soul.

00:54:37.400 --> 00:54:41.440
What I want is...

00:54:42.690 --> 00:54:47.450
We want the <i>Notes</i> to be destroyed.

00:54:52.290 --> 00:54:56.000
Friday, analyze <i>Victor's Notes</i>!

00:55:16.560 --> 00:55:18.850
Watson! What're you doing?!

00:55:19.060 --> 00:55:22.150
Is this some kind of code?

00:55:23.320 --> 00:55:26.360
Where does it describe how to reproduce a soul?!

00:55:31.160 --> 00:55:34.450
Watson, hurry and wrap things up!

00:55:47.670 --> 00:55:49.180
Watson!

00:55:57.730 --> 00:55:59.140
Is it finished?

00:56:17.790 --> 00:56:20.210
The corpses stopped moving?

00:56:22.290 --> 00:56:23.710
Friday!

00:56:26.550 --> 00:56:30.180
The time has come! We need to leave!

00:56:30.380 --> 00:56:32.090
What's wrong, Friday?!

00:56:38.600 --> 00:56:40.810
Can you see me?!

00:56:46.520 --> 00:56:48.110
Friday!

00:56:48.320 --> 00:56:50.240
Watson, we're getting out of here!

00:56:52.450 --> 00:56:54.570
We'll use the cable car inspection corridor!

00:56:54.780 --> 00:56:56.660
Answer me! Friday!

00:57:01.960 --> 00:57:03.830
Tell me you can hear me!

00:57:06.210 --> 00:57:08.300
Watson! What're you doing?!

00:57:11.470 --> 00:57:14.720
I'm here. I'm right here!

00:57:18.600 --> 00:57:20.060
Hey, Watson!

00:57:23.140 --> 00:57:23.770
Friday!

00:57:23.980 --> 00:57:26.230
What's the matter? Pull yourself together!

00:57:29.110 --> 00:57:31.070
What're you doing?! Let him go!

00:57:31.690 --> 00:57:33.030
What about destroying the <i>Notes</i>?!

00:57:33.240 --> 00:57:35.280
Friday analyzed them!

00:57:35.490 --> 00:57:39.370
He's trying to speak! He might have his soul back!

00:57:39.580 --> 00:57:42.460
It just looks like an update error to me.

00:57:42.660 --> 00:57:43.710
Stand aside!

00:57:43.920 --> 00:57:44.870
No!

00:57:45.080 --> 00:57:49.380
What did Karamazov tell you?! Don't you dare say you forgot!

00:57:49.590 --> 00:57:53.720
Are you trying to render his and Nikolai's lives meaningless?!

00:57:54.840 --> 00:57:57.220
You're just seeing what you want to see!

00:57:57.430 --> 00:57:58.600
Move it!

00:57:58.810 --> 00:58:00.770
The world's better off without this thing!

00:58:00.970 --> 00:58:05.270
Stop! That's where Friday's soul is!

00:58:07.610 --> 00:58:11.530
If this is what it means to reproduce a soul...

00:58:11.730 --> 00:58:13.860
then put an end to the suffering!

00:58:26.880 --> 00:58:28.880
Friday...

00:58:29.090 --> 00:58:33.090
Protect... the <i>Notes</i>...

00:58:36.800 --> 00:58:39.430
Foolish humans.

00:58:39.640 --> 00:58:43.850
Why do you go to such lengths to pursue Victor's technology?

00:58:50.650 --> 00:58:55.530
You're arrogant dreamers, and therefore narrow-minded.

00:58:56.610 --> 00:59:02.040
You in particular are much like Victor Frankenstein.

00:59:04.160 --> 00:59:05.620
The One!

00:59:09.040 --> 00:59:11.380
I have no name.

00:59:11.590 --> 00:59:13.800
Because for a hundred years,

00:59:14.010 --> 00:59:18.470
I've been the sole being that's never given one.

00:59:23.680 --> 00:59:25.390
Interesting.

00:59:25.600 --> 00:59:28.650
It seems your master thinks you can be brought back to life

00:59:28.850 --> 00:59:32.730
with Victor's technology.

00:59:34.820 --> 00:59:37.700
Give back... the <i>Notes</i>!

00:59:37.900 --> 00:59:43.830
I wonder, will you go down the same path as Victor?

00:59:46.500 --> 00:59:48.120
Let's go.

00:59:51.960 --> 00:59:53.750
G-Give them back!

01:00:06.310 --> 01:00:07.730
Friday...

01:00:10.600 --> 01:00:15.230
Was your theory... correct?

01:00:20.610 --> 01:00:26.830
Sorry I... couldn't keep... my promise.

01:00:44.930 --> 01:00:48.470
Looks like I'm finally going to die.

01:00:48.680 --> 01:00:50.230
What are you saying?

01:00:51.390 --> 01:00:52.770
Cut that out!

01:00:52.980 --> 01:00:54.400
Let's continue the research.

01:00:54.610 --> 01:01:00.070
I can't prove the existence of the lost 21g soul without you!

01:01:01.530 --> 01:01:05.200
I'll leave this place to you.

01:01:05.410 --> 01:01:07.870
Take over, once I'm gone.

01:01:09.330 --> 01:01:13.920
Break into my grave, and use my dead body.

01:01:16.170 --> 01:01:20.300
If I sense a soul, I'll give you a signal.

01:01:22.510 --> 01:01:24.840
Like this.

01:01:27.140 --> 01:01:30.180
Then our theory will be proven.

01:01:32.350 --> 01:01:33.940
It's a promise.

01:01:43.200 --> 01:01:47.830
Everyone is dead because you didn't keep your promise.

01:01:48.030 --> 01:01:52.250
You're fascinated by the idea of doing whatever you please

01:01:52.460 --> 01:01:56.460
with human souls, and though you know it's taboo, you can't let go.

01:01:58.380 --> 01:02:00.800
You took something you couldn't restore,

01:02:01.010 --> 01:02:04.970
and destroyed it in an irredeemable form.

01:02:05.180 --> 01:02:08.640
A pattern no one can put together.

01:02:08.850 --> 01:02:12.350
You crudely jabbed your finger at the fabric

01:02:12.560 --> 01:02:15.440
of the cleverly constructed soul.

01:02:21.650 --> 01:02:23.070
Friday!

01:02:23.280 --> 01:02:24.490
No!

01:02:24.700 --> 01:02:27.530
Dr. Watson! It isn't safe here!

01:02:28.320 --> 01:02:30.120
- Friday!
- Dr. Watson!

01:02:30.330 --> 01:02:31.830
Friday!

01:02:42.760 --> 01:02:45.090
Dr. Watson.

01:02:45.300 --> 01:02:47.220
Are you all right?

01:02:49.180 --> 01:02:51.310
You mustn't get up.

01:02:51.510 --> 01:02:53.680
You still need rest.

01:02:55.730 --> 01:02:57.560
Where am I?

01:02:57.770 --> 01:03:00.110
On board the <i>Richmond</i>.

01:03:01.770 --> 01:03:05.530
We're currently en route to the States.

01:03:06.780 --> 01:03:11.200
Were you... after the <i>Notes</i>, too?

01:03:12.330 --> 01:03:15.330
I owe you an apology.

01:03:15.540 --> 01:03:19.210
I ended up using a powerful drug to stop him.

01:03:19.420 --> 01:03:22.960
He couldn't be stopped, by my power.

01:03:26.760 --> 01:03:29.430
What about Burnaby?

01:03:29.640 --> 01:03:33.890
Don't worry. He's on board too.

01:03:34.100 --> 01:03:36.930
Mr. Yamazawa is also safe.

01:03:37.140 --> 01:03:39.980
But of course, he's in Japan.

01:03:40.190 --> 01:03:41.860
Am I...?

01:03:42.060 --> 01:03:46.070
The ship's doctor says you were infected with cholera.

01:03:46.280 --> 01:03:50.200
I must have gotten it from the new model corpses at Osato Chemicals.

01:03:52.160 --> 01:03:55.500
You'd best be careful you don't catch it.

01:03:55.700 --> 01:03:57.540
I'll be fine.

01:03:59.210 --> 01:04:02.540
It won't be long before you're back on your feet.

01:04:02.750 --> 01:04:05.300
For now, please just take it easy.

01:04:08.510 --> 01:04:11.510
Thank you, Hadaly.

01:04:26.230 --> 01:04:29.400
The One bears a grudge against humans.

01:04:30.740 --> 01:04:36.450
He was created by human greed, then selfishly cast aside.

01:04:36.660 --> 01:04:39.580
Hatred and loneliness are the forces that move him,

01:04:39.790 --> 01:04:43.920
things that regular corpses don't feel.

01:04:44.130 --> 01:04:47.170
He's using analytical engines and the <i>Notes</i>

01:04:47.380 --> 01:04:52.890
to cause large-scale corpse rampages all over Asia and Europe.

01:04:53.720 --> 01:04:56.510
Now that The One has <i>Victor's Notes</i>, we can't afford

01:04:56.720 --> 01:05:00.940
to let him endlessly disseminate dangerous technology.

01:05:02.440 --> 01:05:07.650
I want you to persuade Dr. Watson to repair his puppet.

01:05:07.860 --> 01:05:10.440
What would be the point of fixing Friday?

01:05:11.860 --> 01:05:15.740
We recovered this writing ball from Osato Chemicals.

01:05:15.950 --> 01:05:21.580
I want Dr. Watson to analyze the traces left on it by The One.

01:05:24.210 --> 01:05:27.210
Sorry, but I can't go along with that.

01:05:27.420 --> 01:05:30.260
You should try asking him yourself.

01:05:30.460 --> 01:05:31.970
Ladies first.

01:05:35.090 --> 01:05:38.850
But hey, I <i>will</i> pay you back for saving me.

01:05:40.560 --> 01:05:43.480
Hey, you there! Hand over the mop!

01:05:44.810 --> 01:05:48.070
Think we can win over the doctor?

01:05:49.530 --> 01:05:52.490
If we don't hurry, the old man will get away.

01:06:03.580 --> 01:06:07.040
That look I saw on your face in Japan was the real thing.

01:06:11.510 --> 01:06:15.260
You must have successfully analyzed the <i>Notes</i>.

01:06:15.470 --> 01:06:21.140
But ever since, no matter how much I fine-tune your necroware,

01:06:21.350 --> 01:06:23.600
the old you won't come back.

01:06:27.900 --> 01:06:33.070
What I'm doing is only making you suffer, isn't it?

01:06:47.460 --> 01:06:53.420
What is Friday, to you? A friend? A test subject?

01:06:53.630 --> 01:06:58.390
I don't know whether Aleksei and Nikolai were right.

01:06:58.590 --> 01:07:02.720
But they risked their lives to pay their debt!

01:07:02.930 --> 01:07:06.390
And yet what about you?! What've you done?!

01:07:08.770 --> 01:07:13.400
Quit obsessing over the dead.

01:07:30.040 --> 01:07:37.380
Paul Bunyan, one of the Eight Great Analytical Engines.

01:07:38.630 --> 01:07:44.810
Your mechanical brain thinks by using steam and electricity.

01:07:45.020 --> 01:07:52.310
And, a captive of the over-installation of the language of corpses, it dreams incoherently.

01:07:53.570 --> 01:07:55.860
Awaken...

01:07:56.070 --> 01:08:00.160
Transmit my words to all the corpses,

01:08:00.360 --> 01:08:06.040
and release them from the truth that they were once human.

01:08:29.940 --> 01:08:31.600
Looks like we weren't fast enough.

01:08:33.400 --> 01:08:36.940
It isn't safe here. Get ready to escape.

01:08:40.150 --> 01:08:41.570
I'm sorry.

01:08:54.340 --> 01:08:55.800
Let's go.

01:09:19.610 --> 01:09:21.820
It's not here, either...

01:09:22.030 --> 01:09:24.370
Where did they hide it?

01:09:30.830 --> 01:09:33.830
The One's taken over Paul Bunyan, too.

01:09:37.420 --> 01:09:40.880
He now controls every place the sound waves reach.

01:09:41.090 --> 01:09:42.930
Sound waves?

01:09:44.300 --> 01:09:45.680
What the hell's going on?!

01:09:45.890 --> 01:09:47.300
Son of a bitch!

01:09:57.310 --> 01:09:59.070
What does The One want?

01:09:59.280 --> 01:10:01.780
The President says it's revenge against humanity,

01:10:01.990 --> 01:10:05.700
but it looks to me like The One is searching for something.

01:10:20.670 --> 01:10:23.760
The answer to that, the answer I desired,

01:10:23.970 --> 01:10:27.050
and your answer are probably all right there.

01:10:28.050 --> 01:10:29.890
Use this if he grows violent.

01:10:30.100 --> 01:10:32.890
I can't stop him with <i>my</i> power.

01:10:39.520 --> 01:10:40.940
Come on!

01:10:42.570 --> 01:10:46.410
The One got to the States a step ahead of us.

01:10:46.610 --> 01:10:52.080
Great Britain, Egypt, India, Afghanistan, Japan.

01:10:53.450 --> 01:10:57.290
We searched for signs of him and the <i>Notes</i> all around the world,

01:10:57.500 --> 01:10:59.460
but we couldn't catch him.

01:11:01.090 --> 01:11:02.920
Dr. Watson.

01:11:03.130 --> 01:11:07.510
Your determination alone finally reached The One and the <i>Notes</i>.

01:11:09.220 --> 01:11:11.510
Taking advantage of the confusion, are we?

01:11:16.310 --> 01:11:19.940
The living can't be controlled the way corpses can.

01:11:20.150 --> 01:11:24.490
But that's not the case for you, Hadaly.

01:11:24.690 --> 01:11:27.780
Bring that over here.

01:11:38.460 --> 01:11:39.880
Fire!

01:11:40.710 --> 01:11:42.800
The soul is 21 grams.

01:11:43.000 --> 01:11:45.920
Then what is the source of that mass?

01:11:46.130 --> 01:11:49.430
You came close to the answer.

01:11:50.760 --> 01:11:53.010
I want a soul!

01:11:53.760 --> 01:11:55.470
I want a soul so I can shed tears,

01:11:55.680 --> 01:11:59.560
so I'll feel sadness, pain, and the like.

01:12:01.610 --> 01:12:04.270
Please! Take me with you!

01:12:10.360 --> 01:12:12.320
Now we're even.

01:12:17.290 --> 01:12:19.040
Damn it! Don't let them escape!

01:12:19.250 --> 01:12:20.670
Hold on!

01:12:21.790 --> 01:12:27.590
Hadaly! Puppets don't get to have dreams!

01:12:42.000 --> 01:12:46.550
San Francisco, 1879

01:12:45.190 --> 01:12:48.860
Hadaly, can you manipulate corpses?

01:12:49.070 --> 01:12:51.990
By using special words, yes.

01:12:52.200 --> 01:12:54.870
So that's what those sound waves are.

01:12:55.080 --> 01:12:59.040
Necroware, analytical engines, even society itself.

01:12:59.250 --> 01:13:04.250
Every complex pattern is sure to have security holes.

01:13:04.460 --> 01:13:08.050
And you and The One can attack those?

01:13:08.260 --> 01:13:10.630
Aren't we going to stop The One?

01:13:10.840 --> 01:13:12.550
Paul Bunyan's over that way.

01:13:12.760 --> 01:13:14.890
I don't think he's there anymore.

01:13:15.100 --> 01:13:16.510
Huh?

01:13:18.100 --> 01:13:23.020
Dr. Watson. I have a safe house beneath the lighthouse.

01:13:23.230 --> 01:13:25.650
Let's regroup there.

01:13:33.240 --> 01:13:34.660
Hang on!

01:13:49.880 --> 01:13:51.300
Friday!

01:13:54.760 --> 01:13:56.180
Shit!

01:14:06.230 --> 01:14:10.150
This is... what Aleksei spoke of...

01:14:11.320 --> 01:14:14.570
The reality that lies... beyond the <i>Notes</i>...

01:14:16.820 --> 01:14:18.330
Dr. Watson!

01:14:18.530 --> 01:14:20.080
Use the drug!

01:14:22.790 --> 01:14:24.710
Up ahead!

01:14:24.920 --> 01:14:27.630
There are lots of them! Can we get past?!

01:14:32.880 --> 01:14:34.380
Here we go!

01:15:01.450 --> 01:15:03.790
Friday! Stop it!

01:15:09.710 --> 01:15:11.210
Hurry, this way!

01:15:15.550 --> 01:15:18.260
Go on ahead.

01:15:18.470 --> 01:15:20.050
What about you?

01:15:20.260 --> 01:15:22.010
I'll buy us time here.

01:15:22.220 --> 01:15:23.680
But...!

01:15:31.980 --> 01:15:34.860
I practically caused this situation.

01:15:35.070 --> 01:15:35.900
Hurry and go!

01:15:36.110 --> 01:15:37.490
I can't leave you two behind!

01:15:37.700 --> 01:15:40.950
Leave this to us, and hurry to the safe house.

01:15:42.080 --> 01:15:45.830
Aleksei asked me if I was prepared!

01:15:46.040 --> 01:15:49.290
Whether I was going to proceed, no matter what reality awaited!

01:15:50.420 --> 01:15:53.050
If I'd only realized what his words meant...!

01:15:54.670 --> 01:15:57.260
Hadaly! Please!

01:16:02.430 --> 01:16:03.930
Are you...?

01:16:06.230 --> 01:16:09.690
I am... an automaton.

01:16:11.810 --> 01:16:16.240
What you need to do right now is determine where The One is.

01:16:16.440 --> 01:16:18.820
We'll catch up to you soon.

01:16:19.780 --> 01:16:25.740
Pursue The One, and teach me the secrets of the soul.

01:16:25.950 --> 01:16:27.580
It's a promise.

01:16:49.390 --> 01:16:52.150
I thought when I got my hands on <i>Victor's Notes</i>,

01:16:52.350 --> 01:16:55.730
I could at last fulfill my promise to you.

01:17:03.370 --> 01:17:09.870
I wanted to fulfill that promise, no matter what I had to do.

01:17:26.220 --> 01:17:30.480
Friday, what are you seeing right now?

01:17:33.690 --> 01:17:37.190
Your soul... Where is it?!

01:17:37.400 --> 01:17:39.610
Friday!

01:17:39.820 --> 01:17:45.070
I just... wanted to see you again!

01:17:45.280 --> 01:17:49.580
I wanted to hear what else you had to say!

01:17:53.040 --> 01:17:54.460
Why?!

01:17:56.250 --> 01:17:58.960
Why'd you leave me?!

01:17:59.170 --> 01:18:01.420
Why won't you come back?!

01:18:12.100 --> 01:18:13.600
Friday!

01:18:19.230 --> 01:18:22.400
Do you... recognize me?!

01:18:22.610 --> 01:18:24.030
Friday!

01:18:38.590 --> 01:18:39.840
I knew it...

01:18:40.050 --> 01:18:43.760
You're in there... aren't you?

01:20:39.040 --> 01:20:40.330
That's far enough!

01:20:40.540 --> 01:20:42.080
We're taking the <i>Notes</i>.

01:20:46.210 --> 01:20:48.170
You're here sooner than I expected.

01:20:48.380 --> 01:20:49.800
Don't move!

01:21:08.820 --> 01:21:12.820
I've been hoping to meet you, The One.

01:21:13.030 --> 01:21:16.330
Walsingham... M, eh?

01:21:16.540 --> 01:21:21.000
I can see the <i>Notes</i> didn't grant you your wish.

01:21:21.210 --> 01:21:23.880
Using analytical engines all over the world...

01:21:24.080 --> 01:21:26.130
Sending corpses on rampages...

01:21:26.340 --> 01:21:28.550
What were you trying to find?

01:21:32.630 --> 01:21:33.970
Well, whatever.

01:21:34.180 --> 01:21:38.810
So long as I have you and these <i>Notes</i>, my wish will come true.

01:21:40.230 --> 01:21:43.270
What will you do with the <i>Notes</i>?

01:21:44.730 --> 01:21:50.190
I'll lead mankind to perfection, to a world without conflict.

01:21:50.400 --> 01:21:54.530
That arrogance will be your undoing.

01:21:56.910 --> 01:21:58.450
Take him away.

01:22:27.270 --> 01:22:28.940
I'm glad you're okay.

01:22:31.780 --> 01:22:33.650
I'm sorry.

01:22:33.860 --> 01:22:35.740
I was mistaken.

01:22:37.950 --> 01:22:39.910
What do you mean, "sorry"?!

01:22:40.120 --> 01:22:42.000
What good's an apology <i>now</i>?!

01:22:42.200 --> 01:22:47.500
If you had destroyed the <i>Notes</i> that time, things wouldn't be like this!

01:22:48.960 --> 01:22:53.670
Women, children, old people! They all died!

01:22:53.880 --> 01:22:56.550
Because of your ambition!

01:22:59.180 --> 01:23:00.600
Damn it!

01:23:01.680 --> 01:23:04.890
What do we do...?

01:23:05.100 --> 01:23:07.810
I don't feel I'm blameless.

01:23:08.020 --> 01:23:10.610
If you say I'm better off dead, then kill me!

01:23:12.860 --> 01:23:16.990
Just... if you'll allow it,

01:23:17.200 --> 01:23:20.030
give me the chance to fulfill my promise to Aleksei and Nikolai!

01:23:21.330 --> 01:23:26.210
Let me put a stop to this chaos! Burnaby!

01:23:31.040 --> 01:23:35.970
How, when you don't even know where he is?

01:23:36.170 --> 01:23:40.640
Friday, bring it here. Show it to Burnaby.

01:23:47.060 --> 01:23:50.190
It's a letter of invitation from The One.

01:23:56.190 --> 01:23:57.900
Is it genuine?

01:23:58.110 --> 01:24:03.160
Yes, it was sent directly to the writing ball as an encoded transmission.

01:24:04.620 --> 01:24:08.370
The One is being transported to the Tower of London.

01:24:08.580 --> 01:24:11.210
M is planning to do something dreadful

01:24:11.420 --> 01:24:14.210
using the power of the <i>Notes</i>.

01:24:14.420 --> 01:24:18.590
I expect he's going to use Charles Babbage to analyze The One.

01:24:22.050 --> 01:24:26.060
I never thought we'd end up fighting Walsingham.

01:24:27.430 --> 01:24:29.140
Do you have a plan?

01:24:29.350 --> 01:24:32.020
I customized Friday for communications use.

01:24:32.230 --> 01:24:35.440
We'll use him to construct a logic maze inside the analytical engine.

01:24:35.650 --> 01:24:40.320
It'll form a siege ring, and contain the melody from spreading.

01:24:40.530 --> 01:24:43.700
That's why it can't be done remotely.

01:24:43.910 --> 01:24:45.910
You're going to go charging in there?

01:24:46.120 --> 01:24:49.460
Burnaby, I want you to help me!

01:24:52.670 --> 01:24:54.670
I had planned to from the start.

01:24:59.170 --> 01:25:00.800
Thank you.

01:25:10.020 --> 01:25:11.560
What's this place?

01:25:11.770 --> 01:25:15.110
An underground facility my father built for experiments.

01:25:15.320 --> 01:25:16.820
Your father?

01:25:22.700 --> 01:25:25.740
What is <i>that</i>?

01:25:25.950 --> 01:25:28.040
The USS Nautilus.

01:25:29.080 --> 01:25:32.960
It was seized in secret from Great Britain on the president's orders,

01:25:33.170 --> 01:25:35.460
and my father remodeled it.

01:25:36.800 --> 01:25:39.010
With this state-of-the-art ship,

01:25:39.210 --> 01:25:43.050
I think we can catch up to The One before things happen.

01:25:45.680 --> 01:25:48.260
You're leaving already?

01:25:48.470 --> 01:25:52.440
I think my spirit world communicator is nearly complete.

01:25:52.640 --> 01:25:54.650
Would you like to see it, first?

01:25:56.310 --> 01:25:58.730
I will, once I return from this trip.

01:26:00.110 --> 01:26:02.200
All right.

01:26:02.400 --> 01:26:06.030
Hadaly, I'll keep this quiet from the government.

01:26:06.240 --> 01:26:10.330
Give your all to what you believe in.

01:26:17.250 --> 01:26:19.590
Thomas Edison...

01:26:19.800 --> 01:26:25.050
Does your father know what it is you seek?

01:26:25.260 --> 01:26:30.470
Yes. But Father does not approve of noise.

01:26:30.680 --> 01:26:32.350
Noise?

01:26:32.560 --> 01:26:35.270
What is the source of the soul's mass?

01:26:35.480 --> 01:26:41.820
The weight of intent. The weight of thought. The strength of ideas.

01:26:42.030 --> 01:26:48.620
I was built to eliminate the "noisy emotions" born of those things.

01:26:48.830 --> 01:26:54.040
Maybe it's that he didn't want to see you sad, or in pain.

01:26:54.250 --> 01:26:57.880
But that's exactly what I want to experience.

01:26:59.290 --> 01:27:00.840
That's why I'm...

01:27:03.840 --> 01:27:05.760
...a failure.

01:27:33.950 --> 01:27:37.580
Analysis of the <i>Notes</i> and of the information in your brain

01:27:37.790 --> 01:27:40.340
is complete.

01:27:41.170 --> 01:27:44.800
All that's left to do now is enter the release code.

01:27:45.880 --> 01:27:48.130
Victor's brain...

01:27:49.590 --> 01:27:52.220
So that's where it was, after all.

01:27:52.430 --> 01:27:57.690
Will we be killed by corpses, or will people kill each other?

01:27:57.890 --> 01:28:01.730
Humanity is doomed either way, at this rate.

01:28:01.940 --> 01:28:04.980
I will save mankind from its destruction.

01:28:06.070 --> 01:28:09.610
Humanity will progress to a new stage!

01:28:24.130 --> 01:28:26.800
Charles Babbage!

01:28:27.010 --> 01:28:31.640
Guide all mankind to its salvation!

01:29:09.130 --> 01:29:10.590
Looks like they know we're here.

01:29:10.800 --> 01:29:14.260
They came to meet us, huh? Nice gesture.

01:29:14.470 --> 01:29:16.430
We'll go via the shortest route.

01:29:16.640 --> 01:29:18.680
It might be a bumpy ride, though.

01:29:18.890 --> 01:29:20.310
We'll leave that to you.

01:29:23.600 --> 01:29:25.190
Everything's set up.

01:29:25.400 --> 01:29:27.820
Make me proud, Friday!

01:29:29.030 --> 01:29:30.490
We're surfacing!

01:29:39.250 --> 01:29:41.660
It's already begun.

01:29:45.000 --> 01:29:47.750
They sure went heavy on the defense.

01:29:49.130 --> 01:29:51.420
Objective: Traitors' Gate!

01:29:52.380 --> 01:29:53.890
We'll force our way through!

01:30:15.490 --> 01:30:20.040
Statesmen of the past also aspired to a world without conflict.

01:30:20.240 --> 01:30:21.950
To protect the people of their country,

01:30:22.160 --> 01:30:25.290
they plunged into the morass of war.

01:30:27.920 --> 01:30:31.510
We invade other countries to protect peace within our own.

01:30:31.710 --> 01:30:33.420
We can't distinguish between the power to protect,

01:30:33.630 --> 01:30:35.680
and the power to plunder.

01:30:35.890 --> 01:30:38.930
Even when we realize it's a mistake, we can't stop.

01:30:39.140 --> 01:30:41.560
That is humanity.

01:30:41.770 --> 01:30:43.640
Go on ahead!

01:30:43.850 --> 01:30:45.060
What about you?!

01:30:45.270 --> 01:30:47.520
I'll cut off the Tower of London's power!

01:30:47.730 --> 01:30:49.360
That's not possible, alone!

01:30:50.440 --> 01:30:54.530
My arms are a lot stronger than yours!

01:30:54.740 --> 01:30:59.660
Now go. We can save the world if we stick to your plan, right?

01:31:04.750 --> 01:31:06.290
Let's hurry!

01:31:12.050 --> 01:31:13.710
Take care.

01:31:16.720 --> 01:31:20.850
This is one of those times I wish you guys understood.

01:31:21.060 --> 01:31:23.640
The <i>mood</i>, that is.

01:31:29.270 --> 01:31:31.820
So, it's despair?

01:31:32.020 --> 01:31:34.150
It's guidance!

01:31:34.360 --> 01:31:37.910
Everyone losing the ability to feel despair

01:31:38.110 --> 01:31:40.990
is one realization of supreme bliss.

01:31:43.040 --> 01:31:47.830
Then there'll be no more conflict, hatred, or killing.

01:31:48.040 --> 01:31:52.000
Because there'll no longer be any way to know what conflict is.

01:31:52.750 --> 01:31:55.630
M is trying to use Aleksei's technology

01:31:55.840 --> 01:31:59.180
to rob people of their will!

01:31:59.390 --> 01:32:02.600
I don't want a world like that.

01:32:02.810 --> 01:32:06.640
I want to know joy via a soul, not a program.

01:32:07.690 --> 01:32:10.610
- Isn't it because sadness and pain exist that you feel joy?

01:32:10.610 --> 01:32:12.940
- Outta my way!
- Isn't it because sadness and pain exist that you feel joy?

01:32:16.690 --> 01:32:18.110
Let's go!

01:32:30.170 --> 01:32:36.880
We'll soon arrive at the ultimate world the will of mankind couldn't reach.

01:32:38.670 --> 01:32:44.560
Amongst all the souls in existence shall I find it.

01:32:44.760 --> 01:32:48.730
A pure soul. A gentle smile.

01:32:50.060 --> 01:32:55.320
A corpse mustn't have a soul or a will.

01:32:56.280 --> 01:33:01.740
M, you're simply a foolish human who pretends to be all-powerful.

01:33:01.950 --> 01:33:06.240
Just like Victor Frankenstein.

01:33:06.450 --> 01:33:10.500
Oh, don't worry. I'll use <i>your</i> soul, too.

01:33:12.630 --> 01:33:15.670
M! Stop Charles Babbage!

01:33:20.800 --> 01:33:23.970
It's been a long time, John Watson.

01:33:25.930 --> 01:33:29.640
Your talent and passion are admirable.

01:33:29.850 --> 01:33:33.560
You pursued Karamazov, located the <i>Notes</i>,

01:33:33.770 --> 01:33:37.150
and even finally made your way here.

01:33:38.440 --> 01:33:43.030
But your mission is already complete.

01:33:43.240 --> 01:33:46.830
I'm putting an end to all your schemes!

01:33:47.030 --> 01:33:48.580
Kill him.

01:33:53.620 --> 01:33:56.290
M! You're making a mistake!

01:33:57.500 --> 01:33:59.130
A mistake?

01:33:59.340 --> 01:34:03.970
It's foolish humans who keep quarreling who are mistaken.

01:34:04.180 --> 01:34:07.470
What about the things people have created through human will?!

01:34:07.680 --> 01:34:10.930
Should all beauty and sublimity vanish,

01:34:11.140 --> 01:34:16.110
the ability to understand them will also be gone.

01:34:18.400 --> 01:34:19.480
Where's the problem?

01:34:19.690 --> 01:34:22.490
People can't abandon their acts of cruelty,

01:34:22.700 --> 01:34:25.950
so they'd probably destroy them on their own anyway.

01:34:26.660 --> 01:34:30.870
We should end it here and now, John Watson!

01:34:31.080 --> 01:34:35.210
You just think you know everything about the world!

01:34:40.250 --> 01:34:44.010
Beauty and sublimity aren't what shape the future!

01:34:44.220 --> 01:34:48.930
It's the willpower to try to actualize one's words

01:34:49.140 --> 01:34:50.930
and feelings for someone else!

01:34:57.270 --> 01:34:58.360
I've stopped The One!

01:34:58.560 --> 01:35:00.150
It'll work now!

01:35:02.900 --> 01:35:05.570
Friday! Form the cage!

01:35:07.030 --> 01:35:10.280
Output at full blast! Suppress the sound waves!

01:35:13.910 --> 01:35:16.000
Hadaly Lilith.

01:35:16.210 --> 01:35:20.800
I'm well aware of what it is you seek.

01:35:21.000 --> 01:35:22.460
Don't resist.

01:35:33.310 --> 01:35:36.060
Watch out behind you.

01:35:39.690 --> 01:35:42.360
- Don't... interfere!

01:35:42.360 --> 01:35:43.940
- Stop!
- Don't... interfere!

01:35:46.320 --> 01:35:47.780
Hadaly!

01:35:59.460 --> 01:36:03.920
Thanks for your trouble. I'll take over from here.

01:36:04.130 --> 01:36:06.380
The One...!

01:36:16.680 --> 01:36:19.310
Friday! Take it offline!

01:36:23.070 --> 01:36:27.110
I believed in your determination,

01:36:27.320 --> 01:36:29.990
John Watson.

01:36:39.830 --> 01:36:45.670
You sought the <i>Notes</i>, and you sought the soul.

01:36:45.880 --> 01:36:50.590
Then at last, fate led you here.

01:36:55.180 --> 01:36:59.810
Along with two vessels for souls.

01:37:00.020 --> 01:37:01.150
Get real!

01:37:01.350 --> 01:37:04.190
You're saying this has all happened the way you wanted?!

01:37:08.360 --> 01:37:10.570
The time has come.

01:37:19.540 --> 01:37:24.960
Where did the soul come to be, and how?

01:37:28.670 --> 01:37:30.170
Damn it!

01:37:30.380 --> 01:37:34.800
In the creation of that soul lies the essence

01:37:35.010 --> 01:37:38.810
of the forbidden art Victor sealed away.

01:37:49.440 --> 01:37:57.120
I will show you the moment when life... when the soul is born.

01:38:10.590 --> 01:38:13.340
Victor Frankenstein.

01:38:13.550 --> 01:38:19.560
My bride's soul is sealed within the depths of your consciousness.

01:38:19.770 --> 01:38:21.890
I'm taking it back.

01:38:37.410 --> 01:38:41.870
Friday! Hadaly! I'm coming to resc--

01:38:43.080 --> 01:38:46.170
The giant analytical engines that understand the language of corpses,

01:38:46.380 --> 01:38:51.840
and that are linked to corpses worldwide,

01:38:52.050 --> 01:38:57.090
now form their very consciousness.

01:38:57.300 --> 01:39:00.930
There's no longer any need to describe words on punch cards,

01:39:01.140 --> 01:39:06.600
connect cables, and perform installations.

01:39:08.860 --> 01:39:15.610
For what we're witnessing is the materialization of language itself.

01:39:20.580 --> 01:39:23.500
Language forms a consciousness,

01:39:23.700 --> 01:39:28.040
one that will weave up my bride's consciousness from the corpses,

01:39:28.250 --> 01:39:31.960
via the analytical engines.

01:39:33.510 --> 01:39:42.470
All wills become one will, and one will becomes all wills.

01:39:42.680 --> 01:39:48.730
All humanity becomes a single soul, just one.

01:39:49.980 --> 01:39:52.940
Hadaly Lilith!

01:39:53.150 --> 01:39:55.860
I give to you a soul.

01:40:01.240 --> 01:40:06.910
The elements composing my bride's soul have been released!

01:40:09.000 --> 01:40:15.510
Become the vessel of my departed bride, and obtain a soul!

01:40:24.010 --> 01:40:28.690
I feel it. Your presence.

01:40:28.890 --> 01:40:32.150
The warmth of your soul.

01:40:33.270 --> 01:40:37.150
You're there, aren't you...

01:40:37.360 --> 01:40:38.530
Stop it!

01:40:38.740 --> 01:40:42.910
What Hadaly wanted was her own joy and sadness!

01:40:43.120 --> 01:40:45.990
A soul to feel those things!

01:40:46.200 --> 01:40:50.620
Not the soul of your <i>bride</i>!

01:40:50.830 --> 01:40:53.460
What a pity.

01:40:53.670 --> 01:40:58.470
I thought I could get you to understand.

01:40:58.670 --> 01:41:04.100
You, who more than any other, longed for the soul.

01:41:06.470 --> 01:41:12.560
Nevertheless... this body has been maintained well.

01:41:16.980 --> 01:41:20.030
It will do nicely, as my vessel.

01:41:27.410 --> 01:41:32.210
Now... awaken.

01:41:32.420 --> 01:41:34.330
My bride.

01:42:15.630 --> 01:42:20.090
Are you able to see me?

01:42:20.300 --> 01:42:23.220
Do you know who I am?

01:42:25.140 --> 01:42:29.100
Smile for me once again.

01:42:47.910 --> 01:42:49.330
Watson!

01:42:50.870 --> 01:42:52.750
The rest is up to you!

01:43:11.100 --> 01:43:14.600
You struggle in vain...!

01:43:24.740 --> 01:43:28.370
Friday, activate the logic maze!

01:43:28.570 --> 01:43:33.080
Lock The One's soul and the corpse language inside the <i>Notes</i>!

01:43:40.000 --> 01:43:41.420
This...

01:43:44.170 --> 01:43:46.380
...is our will!

01:43:48.090 --> 01:43:50.100
Impossible...!

01:45:31.780 --> 01:45:33.200
Dr. Watson.

01:45:35.330 --> 01:45:36.160
Give me your hand.

01:45:36.370 --> 01:45:37.660
Hadaly...

01:45:37.870 --> 01:45:39.450
Thank goodness you're okay!

01:47:24.430 --> 01:47:28.610
The words of his bride entered into me.

01:47:29.690 --> 01:47:34.070
Sadness, anger, and joy.

01:47:35.360 --> 01:47:39.990
I didn't think I could ever be myself again, and that scared me.

01:47:42.580 --> 01:47:44.960
Even though I supposedly have no soul.

01:47:47.250 --> 01:47:49.460
You do have a soul.

01:47:51.920 --> 01:47:56.220
I don't even have any mechanism for shedding tears.

01:47:56.420 --> 01:48:00.600
Hadaly, that's the side of you I always liked.

01:48:17.360 --> 01:48:21.490
If I have a soul, then he has one too.

01:48:25.040 --> 01:48:26.660
Don't give up.

01:48:29.790 --> 01:48:32.840
Thank you, Hadaly.

01:48:35.460 --> 01:48:37.090
That's all over.

01:48:38.800 --> 01:48:41.890
We're home, at any rate.

01:48:42.100 --> 01:48:44.260
What will you do?

01:48:44.470 --> 01:48:46.770
I think I'll do some traveling.

01:48:46.980 --> 01:48:50.400
So don't tell me the whole story.

01:48:50.600 --> 01:48:53.610
Some things, I'm better off not knowing.

01:48:53.820 --> 01:48:55.570
That's true.

01:48:55.780 --> 01:49:00.070
You wouldn't be able to fit it all into that head of yours, anyway.

01:49:00.280 --> 01:49:01.910
You flatter me.

01:49:08.580 --> 01:49:10.040
See you.

01:49:47.160 --> 01:49:54.130
The thing I require, before all else, is a corpse.

01:49:59.130 --> 01:50:01.420
It's been confirmed that when a human dies,

01:50:01.630 --> 01:50:08.180
their body will then weigh 21 grams less than it did while alive.

01:50:10.060 --> 01:50:12.520
That's the weight of the spiritual element,

01:50:12.730 --> 01:50:15.310
the so-called weight of the soul.

01:50:18.730 --> 01:50:24.660
This journey was set in motion when you told me that.

01:50:31.290 --> 01:50:35.330
I still recall your words.

01:50:38.300 --> 01:50:40.920
I was fond of the things you write.

01:50:43.720 --> 01:50:49.810
Your words that were stored within me...

01:50:50.020 --> 01:50:55.020
led me on this journey, and they sustained me.

01:51:01.900 --> 01:51:08.450
Will the words I said... on the journey...

01:51:08.660 --> 01:51:14.160
bring about... anything in you...?

01:51:17.330 --> 01:51:20.800
Friday, will I...

01:51:24.090 --> 01:51:27.140
...be able to see you?

01:51:31.680 --> 01:51:34.680
Will I...

01:51:34.890 --> 01:51:36.980
be able to hear your voice?

01:51:41.020 --> 01:51:43.110
If so, then...

01:51:46.490 --> 01:51:48.070
Friday...

01:51:50.580 --> 01:51:52.120
Once again...

01:51:55.960 --> 01:51:57.460
...we'll...

01:52:33.410 --> 01:52:43.410
<i>kazoeta nokosareta toki o</i>

01:52:33.410 --> 01:52:43.410
<i>I've counted the time left</i>

01:52:44.750 --> 01:52:52.350
<i>soshite me o akeru anata wa</i>

01:52:44.750 --> 01:52:52.350
<i>And when you open your eyes</i>

01:52:52.550 --> 01:53:09.550
<i>yumemita ano hi no basho de negai o togete</i>

01:52:52.550 --> 01:53:09.550
<i>You fulfill our wish, in the place from that day when we dreamed</i>

01:53:18.870 --> 01:53:28.870
<i>tomatta toki o ugokashite</i>

01:53:18.870 --> 01:53:28.870
<i>I'll make time move again</i>

01:53:30.180 --> 01:53:36.350
<i>anata ni aeru wa</i>

01:53:30.180 --> 01:53:36.350
<i>And I'll get to see you</i>

01:53:36.560 --> 01:53:49.400
<i>kurikaeshita asu o owari ni shite</i>

01:53:36.560 --> 01:53:49.400
<i>Putting an end to that endlessly repeating tomorrow</i>

01:53:49.490 --> 01:54:02.490
<i>kono me ni utsushita mirai o anata ni</i>

01:53:49.490 --> 01:54:02.490
<i>The future I've seen, I promise it to you</i>

01:54:02.620 --> 01:54:08.880
<i>yakusoku shite ikite iku no</i>

01:54:02.620 --> 01:54:08.880
<i>I will live on</i>

01:54:09.090 --> 01:54:15.220
<i>furimukazu ni susunde</i>

01:54:09.090 --> 01:54:15.220
<i>Move forward, don't look back</i>

01:54:15.430 --> 01:54:27.050
<i>watashi wa koko ni iru wa anata no omoi ni</i>

01:54:15.430 --> 01:54:27.050
<i>I'm right here in your heart</i>

01:54:27.070 --> 01:54:41.060
<i>yume o mite towa ni nemuru</i>

01:54:27.070 --> 01:54:41.060
<i>I'll sleep and dream here forever</i>

01:54:55.510 --> 01:55:06.610
<i>tobira o akete misete</i>

01:54:55.510 --> 01:55:06.610
<i>Open the door now</i>

01:55:06.810 --> 01:55:20.050
<i>negai wa hitotsu dake kanau</i>

01:55:06.810 --> 01:55:20.050
<i>And one wish will come true</i>

01:55:20.200 --> 01:55:27.540
<i>sono te de tsukande</i>

01:55:20.200 --> 01:55:27.540
<i>Take it in your hand</i>

01:55:27.750 --> 01:55:36.550
<i>mirai o watashi to yakusoku shite</i>

01:55:27.750 --> 01:55:36.550
<i>Promise me the future</i>

01:55:36.760 --> 01:55:39.680
<i>ikite iku no</i>

01:55:36.760 --> 01:55:39.680
<i>You will live on</i>

01:55:39.890 --> 01:55:45.940
<i>furimukazu ni susunde</i>

01:55:39.890 --> 01:55:45.940
<i>Move forward, don't look back</i>

01:55:46.140 --> 01:55:57.600
<i>anata wa koko ni iru wa kuzure ochiru ima</i>

01:55:46.140 --> 01:55:57.600
<i>You're right here in the crumbling present</i>

01:55:57.860 --> 01:56:12.260
<i>yume o mite towa ni nemuru</i>

01:55:57.860 --> 01:56:12.260
<i>I'll sleep and dream forever</i>

01:56:12.500 --> 01:56:28.100
<i>watashi wa iroasezu ni</i>

01:56:12.500 --> 01:56:28.100
<i>Never fading</i>

01:57:05.770 --> 01:57:10.850
Dr. Watson, my pen records thusly.

01:57:11.730 --> 01:57:15.650
He does not reveal himself on this plain.

01:57:17.110 --> 01:57:21.700
He sealed the <i>Notes</i> within his own mind,

01:57:21.910 --> 01:57:24.740
and departed for a horizon of different words.

01:57:26.240 --> 01:57:30.620
The memory of those days spent journeying has been lost.

01:57:32.040 --> 01:57:35.750
I, I ask.

01:57:35.960 --> 01:57:39.380
Do I possess a consciousness?

01:57:39.590 --> 01:57:43.340
I, I reply.

01:57:43.550 --> 01:57:50.560
When did this consciousness come to be, or has that yet to happen?

01:57:50.770 --> 01:57:54.860
There is still so little I understand.

01:57:57.230 --> 01:58:05.200
Dr. Watson, there are many things I have yet to tell you.

01:58:05.410 --> 01:58:10.120
I am here as materialized information.

01:58:11.460 --> 01:58:18.500
Now, the fact that I exist this way is thanks to you.

01:58:20.010 --> 01:58:26.850
If possible, I'd at least like you to hear this one thing.

01:58:27.970 --> 01:58:30.810
May these words materialize,

01:58:31.020 --> 01:58:36.520
and bring new life to the story you left behind.

01:58:38.480 --> 01:58:40.030
Thank you.

01:58:52.060 --> 01:58:55.780
London, 4 years later

01:59:05.050 --> 01:59:06.470
Shit!

01:59:11.600 --> 01:59:13.230
Watson!

01:59:13.430 --> 01:59:14.940
You're late, Holmes!

01:59:28.280 --> 01:59:30.910
How's he doing, Hadaly?

01:59:31.120 --> 01:59:35.210
Woops. You go by "Irene Adler" now.

01:59:37.710 --> 01:59:39.630
The same as ever.

01:59:39.840 --> 01:59:44.970
He's running all around London with his new partner.
